    "description": "Boldyn Networks is a neutral-host digital-infrastructure platform providing distributed antenna systems, private networks, Wi-Fi, fiber and related shared connectivity for transit systems, venues, campuses, cities and mobile carriers. BAI Communications' Northern Hemisphere businesses adopted the Boldyn name in June 2023, and the U.S. regional perimeter—including Mobilitie, Transit Wireless, ZenFi, Signal Point and Apogee—operates within the same manager-level group rather than as a separate portfolio company. CPP Investments has backed predecessor BAI since 2009 and held 86% of Boldyn Networks at the latest direct stake disclosure on March 6, 2024; AIMCo held 10%. Manulife Investment Management retains a separately evidenced minority ownership interest in certain U.S. digital-infrastructure assets through Manulife Infrastructure Fund II, but its exact percentage and investment vehicle are not publicly disclosed. The residual parent equity, AIMCo entry date and later stake changes were not publicly disclosed, and no subsequent exit or signed ownership transfer was identified through September 3, 2026.",
